@1   = ~chriz-bg-kits requires BG2:EE or EET with EEex v1.2.0+ (extra_pattern_dbs + M___EEex.lua).~
@2   = ~chriz-bg-kits replaces ArtisansKitpack and BardicWonders and cannot be installed alongside them.~
@3   = ~Requires Component 100 (Core EEex Kit Kernel) to be installed first.~

@100 = ~Core EEex Kit Kernel (Weapon Usability, Multiclass Kit Proficiencies, Global Non-Warrior Proficiency APR, Bard Spells, Strength Floor)~
@110 = ~Forgotten Realms Racial Class, Kit & Multiclass Rules (Recommended)~
@111 = ~Unlock All Classes, Kits, Dual-Classes & Multiclasses for All Races~
@112 = ~Racial Class, Kit & Multiclass Rules~
@200 = ~Cleric Overhaul: Priest of Tempus~
@2001 = ~Cleric Overhaul: Vanilla Deities (Lathander, Helm, Talos, Tyr)~
@2002 = ~Cleric Kit: Priest of Shar~
@2003 = ~Cleric Kit: Priest of Umberlee~
@2004 = ~Cleric Kit: Priest of Ilmater~
@210 = ~Sorcerer Kit: Stonefire Sorcerer~
@220 = ~Druid Kit: Elementalist~
@300 = ~Standalone Fighter Kit: Bloodrager~
@310 = ~Bard Overhaul: Jester & Skald~
@320 = ~Core Kit & HLA Fixes (Archer Called Shot, Physical Hardiness, Resist Magic, Deathblows, Dual-Class Kit Names)~

@201 = ~Holy Power~
@202 = ~Holy Power
Through this prayer, the Priest of Tempus channels divine battle-prowess, gaining Fighter THAC0 progression, temporary Strength floor scaling up to 21 at level 15 (without lowering stronger Strength buffs), and +1 Hit Point per level (max 20). Does not stack with other transformation magic.~
@203 = ~Chaos of Battle~
@204 = ~Chaos of Battle
The Priest of Tempus unleashes battle-luck across allies (+1 to +3 Luck) while cursing nearby enemies (-1 to -3 THAC0 and Saving Throws, Save vs. Spell negates).~
@205 = ~PRIEST OF TEMPUS: Champions of the Lord of Battles relish honorable melee combat and shun sneaky divination magic.
Advantages:
- Automatically receives 1 Battle Axe proficiency at 1st level in addition to starting pips, and may place 2 pips in Long Sword, Battle Axe, Crossbow, standard cleric weapons, and all fighting styles.
- Gains +1/2 attack per round when wielding a weapon in which the priest holds 2 or more proficiency pips (without double-stacking on Warrior multiclasses).
- Casts Chaos of Battle and an enhanced non-lowering Holy Power.
Disadvantages:
- Divination Toll: Tempus strips all Divination priest spells from the cleric's spellbook.~

@301 = ~Enrage~
@302 = ~Enrage
Enters a blood-fueled frenzy for 5 rounds (+2 melee THAC0, +2 melee damage, -2 Armor Class penalty, +15 temporary Hit Points with no end-of-rage backlash), shielding the mind against Charm, Fear, Hold, Sleep, and Stun. Each melee hit sustains the frenzy up to a 10-round maximum (20 rounds with Extend Rage). When Enrage ends, the Bloodrager is Winded for 5 rounds (-2 THAC0, -2 damage, +2 AC penalty).~
@303 = ~Extend Rage~
@304 = ~Extend Rage (HLA)
Doubles the maximum sustained duration of Enrage from 10 rounds to 20 rounds.~
@305 = ~bloodrager~
@306 = ~Bloodrager~
@307 = ~BLOODRAGER: A savage frontline warrior whose fury intensifies as wounds accumulate.
Advantages:
- In Extremis: Gains +1 melee damage and +1 Save vs. Death at <76%, <50%, and <26% Hit Points (doubled while Enraged); at level 14+, each threshold also grants +5% physical resistance (doubled to +10%/+20%/+30% while Enraged).
- May Enrage 1/day per 4 levels (focused mind-shield, temporary Hit Points, melee-hit duration refresh up to hard cap).
Disadvantages:
- Suffers a permanent -4 THAC0 penalty with ranged weapons.
- Cannot place proficiency pips in or equip ranged missile weapons (Crossbow, Longbow, Shortbow, Dart, Sling).~

@401 = ~Piercing Mockery~
@402 = ~Piercing Mockery
The Jester's song unnerves enemies (Save vs. Spell with scaling penalty up to -4), inflicting Confusion, Slow at high levels, and -1/-2 penalties to THAC0 and Saving Throws.~
@403 = ~Heckle~
@404 = ~Heckle
Mocks a single foe (-2 THAC0, -2 Armor Class, 35% spell failure for 3 rounds, Save vs. Spell negates).~
@405 = ~Mad Ramble~
@406 = ~Mad Ramble
Broadcasts disorienting nonsense around the Jester (25% spell failure and -1 Luck to nearby enemies, Save vs. Spell negates).~
@407 = ~The Fool's Journey~
@408 = ~The Fool's Journey (HLA)
Permanent +1 Luck, +2 Saving Throws, and a non-stacking aura granting allies +1 Luck and +1 THAC0.~
@409 = ~JESTER: Uses biting mockery (Heckle, Mad Ramble, Piercing Mockery) and un-nerfed IWD spell progression up to 7th level.~
@410 = ~SKALD: Inspires allies in combat and may place up to 2 proficiency pips in every weapon and fighting style, while casting BG2 bard spells up to 6th level.~

@501 = ~Hardiness (HLA): Grants 40% resistance to all physical damage types for 1 turn.~
@502 = ~Resist Magic (HLA): Sets Magic Resistance to a minimum floor of 50% for 4 rounds without lowering higher existing Magic Resistance.~
@503 = ~Deathblow (HLA): Automatically slays struck creatures of 12 Hit Dice or fewer for 2 rounds.~
@504 = ~Greater Deathblow (HLA): Automatically slays struck creatures of 16 Hit Dice or fewer for 2 rounds.~

@511 = ~Mage~
@512 = ~Fighter~
@513 = ~Cleric~
@514 = ~Thief~
@515 = ~Druid~
@516 = ~Ranger~
@517 = ~Barbarian~
@521 = ~mage~
@522 = ~fighter~
@523 = ~cleric~
@524 = ~thief~
@525 = ~druid~
@526 = ~ranger~
@527 = ~barbarian~

@2100 = ~stonefire sorcerer~
@2101 = ~Stonefire Sorcerer~
@2102 = ~STONEFIRE SORCERER: Forged in the volcanic hearts of dwarven holds, Stonefire Sorcerers channel the weight of living stone and the fury of magma directly through runic mail and dwarven steel.

Advantages:
- Hit Die: d6.
- May equip and Specialize (2 slots) in Warhammers and Battle Axes, gaining +1/2 attack per round when specialized.
- May wear Helmets, Shields (except Tower Shields), and Armor up to Chain Mail, and casts arcane spells in armor up to Chain Mail without spell failure.
- Immune to Wing Buffet and Knockdown.
- Gains 5% / 10% / 15% / 20% physical damage resistance and 20% / 30% / 40% / 50% Fire resistance at levels 4 / 8 / 12 / 16.
- Gains +1 Constitution at levels 5 and 15.
- May cast Magma Eruption once per day at level 3 (increasing to 2/day at level 9 and 3/day at level 15).

Disadvantages:
- May cast one fewer spell per level per day.
- Barred School: Illusion (cannot learn Illusion spells or read Illusion scrolls).~
@2103 = ~Magma Eruption~
@2104 = ~Magma Eruption
Range: 30 ft.
Area of Effect: Small enemy-only burst
Casting Time: 3
Saving Throw: Breath (1/2 damage; negates Slow)

Calls forth a localized eruption of molten rock and concussive stone at a target point within 30 feet. Enemies caught in the blast suffer 3d6 damage at 3rd level, 5d6 at 9th level, and 7d6 at 15th level (half crushing, half fire; Save vs. Breath for half) and must save vs. Breath or be slowed for 2 rounds.~

@2200 = ~elementalist~
@2201 = ~Elementalist~
@2202 = ~ELEMENTALIST: Forsaking woodland beasts and insect swarms, Elementalist druids commune directly with the four primordial planes of Fire, Water, Air, and Earth.

Advantages:
- +10% baseline resistance to Fire, Cold, Electricity, and Acid.
- Receives a curated bonus Priest spellbook of elemental magic across spell levels 1 through 7.
- Elemental Forms (Fire, Water, Air, Earth): Shared pool of 2 uses/day at 3rd level, 3/day at 7th, 4/day at 10th, and 5/day at 12th+ (scaling at levels 3, 7, 12, and 15). Spellcasting remains fully enabled while transformed:
  * Fire Form: 2 APR slashing + fire natural attack, +25% Fire damage dealt, 50/75/90/100% Fire resistance, 0/10/15/20% physical resistance floor, and a 1d6 fire recoil aura at 12th level.
  * Water Form: 2 APR crushing natural attack, +20% Cold damage dealt, 50/75/90/100% Cold resistance, 0/25/50/50% Fire resistance, 10/15/20/25% physical resistance floor, 0/1/1/2 HP/round regeneration, and Tidal Healing (Cure Wounds spells cast at speed 1, 30-ft. range, and +25% healing).
  * Air Form: 2/3/3/3 APR piercing + electrical natural attack, +3 movement rate, +20% Electricity damage dealt, 50/75/90/100% Electricity resistance, 20/40/50/60% Missile resistance, 0/10/15/20% physical resistance floor, and +1/+2 faster casting speed at levels 12/15.
  * Earth Form: 2 APR heavy crushing natural attack, Strength floor 19/20/21/22 (Dexterity 9), Knockdown/Wing Buffet immunity, 50/75/90/100% Acid resistance, 15/25/35/50% Slashing/Piercing/Missile resistance floor, and 10/15/20/25% Crushing resistance floor.
- High-Level Ability — Primal Penetration: Replaces Elemental Transformation. While in an Elemental Form, the Elementalist's own spells of that form's element pierce half of the target's Magic Resistance and cap non-Elemental targets' elemental resistance at 70%; in Earth Form, melee attacks ignore 25% of target Crushing resistance and have a 20% chance (Save vs. Breath negates) to knock the target down for 1 round.

Disadvantages:
- Cannot wear armor (robes permitted).
- Loses vanilla animal shapeshifting, Animal-sphere summons, and Insect swarm spells (retains Elemental Summonings).~
@2203 = ~Fire Elemental Form~
@2204 = ~Fire Elemental Form
Transforms into a living Flame Elemental (Lesser at 3rd, Standard at 7th, Greater at 12th, Final at 15th). Grants +25% Fire damage dealt, scaling Fire resistance (50/75/90/100%), physical resistance floor (0/10/15/20%), 2 APR slashing/fire melee attacks, and at 12th+ level a 1d6 fire recoil aura plus elemental immunities.~
@2205 = ~Water Elemental Form~
@2206 = ~Water Elemental Form
Transforms into a living Water Elemental. Grants +20% Cold damage dealt, scaling Cold resistance (50/75/90/100%), Fire resistance (0/25/50/50%), physical resistance floor (10/15/20/25%), regeneration (0/1/1/2 HP/round), and Tidal Healing (Cure Wounds spells gain Casting Time 1, 30-ft. range, and +25% extra healing).~
@2207 = ~Air Elemental Form~
@2208 = ~Air Elemental Form
Transforms into a living Air Elemental. Grants +20% Electricity damage dealt, 2/3/3/3 APR piercing/electrical melee attacks, +3 movement rate, scaling Electricity resistance (50/75/90/100%), Missile resistance (20/40/50/60%), physical resistance floor (0/10/15/20%), and +1/+2 faster casting speed at levels 12/15.~
@2209 = ~Earth Elemental Form~
@2210 = ~Earth Elemental Form
Transforms into a living Earth Elemental. Grants Strength floor 19/20/21/22 (Dexterity 9), Knockdown and Wing Buffet immunity, scaling Acid resistance (50/75/90/100%), 15/25/35/50% Slashing/Piercing/Missile resistance floor, and 10/15/20/25% Crushing resistance floor.~
@2211 = ~Natural Form~
@2212 = ~Natural Form
Returns the Elementalist to natural humanoid form.~
@2213 = ~Primal Penetration~
@2214 = ~Primal Penetration (HLA)
One-time passive High-Level Ability. While transformed into an Elemental Form, the Elementalist's own spells matching that form's element (Fire -> Fire, Water -> Cold, Air -> Electricity, Earth -> Acid) pierce half of the target's Magic Resistance and cap non-Elemental targets' elemental resistance at 70%. In Earth Form, Tectonic Strikes ignore 25% of target Crushing resistance and have a 20% chance (Save vs. Breath negates) to knock struck targets down for 1 round.~

@2220 = ~Burning Hands~
@2221 = ~Burning Hands: Releases a searing cone of fire dealing 1d3+4 fire damage (Save vs. Spell for half).~
@2222 = ~Shocking Grasp~
@2223 = ~Shocking Grasp: Jolts a touched enemy for 1d8+4 electrical damage.~
@2224 = ~Agannazar's Scorcher~
@2225 = ~Agannazar's Scorcher: Projects a jet of flame dealing 3d6 fire damage.~
@2226 = ~Melf's Acid Arrow~
@2227 = ~Melf's Acid Arrow: Launches a magical arrow of acid dealing 2d4 acid damage immediately and 2d4 acid damage the following round.~
@2228 = ~Snilloc's Snowball Swarm~
@2229 = ~Snilloc's Snowball Swarm: Unleashes an icy flurry dealing 1d3 cold damage per level (up to 8d3, Save vs. Spell for half) in a 15-ft. radius.~
@2230 = ~Fireball~
@2231 = ~Fireball: Detonates an explosive burst of flame dealing 8d6 fire damage (Save vs. Spell for half).~
@2232 = ~Lightning Bolt~
@2233 = ~Lightning Bolt: Releases a stroke of electrical energy dealing 8d6 electrical damage (Save vs. Spell for half).~
@2234 = ~Icelance~
@2235 = ~Icelance: Hurls a magical lance of ice dealing 5d6 cold damage and stunning the target for 3 rounds unless a Save vs. Spell succeeds.~
@2236 = ~Ice Storm~
@2237 = ~Ice Storm: Pummels an area with giant hailstones for 2d8 cold damage.~
@2238 = ~Vitriolic Sphere~
@2239 = ~Vitriolic Sphere: Hurls a sphere of emerald acid dealing 1d4 acid damage per level (up to 15d4, Save vs. Spell for half) plus 2d4 lingering acid damage on a failed save.~
@2240 = ~Fire Shield (Red)~
@2241 = ~Fire Shield (Red): Wreathes the caster in flames granting +50% Fire resistance and inflicting fire damage on melee attackers.~
@2242 = ~Cone of Cold~
@2243 = ~Cone of Cold: Projects a freezing cone dealing 10d4+10 cold damage (Save vs. Spell for half).~
@2244 = ~Sunfire~
@2245 = ~Sunfire: Releases a globe of searing flame around the caster dealing 10d6 fire damage (Save vs. Spell for half).~
@2246 = ~Chain Lightning~
@2247 = ~Chain Lightning: Arcs electrical bolts across enemies dealing 10d6 electrical damage (Save vs. Spell for half).~
@2248 = ~Otiluke's Freezing Sphere~
@2249 = ~Otiluke's Freezing Sphere: Fires a globe of absolute zero dealing 1d4+2 cold damage per level (Save vs. Spell negates).~
@2250 = ~Delayed Blast Fireball~
@2251 = ~Delayed Blast Fireball: Creates a devastating fireball dealing 14d6 fire damage (Save vs. Spell for half).~
@2252 = ~Acid Storm~
@2253 = ~Acid Storm: Unleashes a downpour of caustic acid over 3 rounds dealing 7d4, 7d6, and 7d8 acid damage (Save vs. Spell for half).~
@2254 = ~Incendiary Cloud~
@2255 = ~Incendiary Cloud: Conjures a billowing cloud of white-hot embers dealing 14d4 fire damage (Save vs. Spell for half).~

// Component 201: Vanilla Deity Clerics (Lathander, Helm, Talos, Tyr) (@2300..@2349)
@2300 = ~Boon of Lathander~
@2301 = ~Boon of Lathander
Duration: 1 round/level
Casting Time: 1

The Priest of Lathander channels the Morninglord's radiance, gaining +1 to THAC0, +1 to damage rolls, +1 to all Saving Throws, +1 extra attack per round (does not stack with Haste or Improved Haste), and immunity to Level Drain for the duration.~
@2302 = ~PRIEST OF LATHANDER: Clerics of the Morninglord are champions of dawn, vitality, and the destruction of undead.
Advantages:
- Automatically receives 1 Mace proficiency pip at 1st level in addition to starting proficiencies.
- May cast Boon of Lathander once per day at 1st level (plus 1 additional use every 5 levels): grants +1 THAC0, +1 damage, +1 to all Saving Throws, +1 extra attack per round (capped vs. Haste/Improved Haste), and immunity to Level Drain for 1 round per level.
- May cast Hold Undead once per day at 1st level (plus 1 additional use every 10 levels).
- Receives a Holy Symbol of Lathander at 25th level.
Disadvantages:
- Alignment restricted to Lawful Good, Neutral Good, Chaotic Good, or True Neutral.~

@2310 = ~Seeking Sword~
@2311 = ~Seeking Sword
Duration: 1 round/level
Casting Time: 5

Summons a +4 Bastard Sword of radiant vigilance into the Priest of Helm's hands. The Seeking Sword deals 2d4 slashing damage, grants 3 base attacks per round and a +2 bonus to Armor Class, and does not restrict spellcasting while equipped. May be dismissed at will via Dismiss Seeking Sword.~
@2312 = ~Seeking Sword~
@2313 = ~This radiant +4 Bastard Sword is summoned by a Priest of Helm to guard the faithful. It sets base attacks per round to 3, grants a +2 bonus to Armor Class, and allows unhindered spellcasting while wielded.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +4
Damage: 2d4 (slashing)
Enchantment: +4
Special:
  3 base attacks per round
  +2 Armor Class
  Spellcasting remains enabled
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: Bastard Sword
Type: One-handed
Weight: 0~
@2314 = ~Dismiss Seeking Sword~
@2315 = ~Dismiss Seeking Sword
Dismisses the summoned Seeking Sword immediately.~
@2316 = ~PRIEST OF HELM: Clerics of the Vigilant One stand watch over their allies with blade and ward alike.
Advantages:
- Automatically receives 1 Bastard Sword proficiency pip at 1st level in addition to starting proficiencies, and may equip and become proficient in Bastard Swords.
- May cast Seeking Sword once per day at 1st level (plus 1 additional use every 10 levels): summons a +4 Bastard Sword (2d4 slashing, 3 base attacks per round, +2 Armor Class) without disabling spellcasting, and may dismiss it at will.
- May cast True Sight once per day at 1st level (plus 1 additional use every 5 levels).
- Receives a Holy Symbol of Helm at 25th level.
Disadvantages:
- Alignment restricted to Lawful Good, Lawful Neutral, True Neutral, or Lawful Evil.~

@2320 = ~Lightning of Talos~
@2321 = ~Lightning of Talos
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant (stagger 1 round)
Casting Time: 2
Saving Throw: Breath (half damage; negates stagger)

Calls down a targeted bolt of lightning upon a single foe, dealing 1d6 electrical damage per caster level (max 10d6; Save vs. Breath for half). A creature that fails its Saving Throw vs. Breath is also staggered for 1 round (-2 THAC0 and -2 Armor Class).~
@2322 = ~PRIEST OF TALOS: Stormlords revel in unleashed fury, wielding thunder, lightning, and the spear of the tempest.
Advantages:
- Automatically receives 1 Spear proficiency pip at 1st level in addition to starting proficiencies, and may equip and become proficient in Spears and Daggers.
- +25% baseline resistance to Electricity.
- May cast Lightning of Talos once per day at 1st level (plus 1 additional use every 5 levels): calls down a targeted, non-bouncing strike for 1d6 electrical damage per level (max 10d6, Save vs. Breath for half) plus a 1-round stagger (-2 THAC0, -2 Armor Class; Save vs. Breath negates).
- May cast Storm Shield once per day at 1st level (plus 1 additional use every 10 levels).
- Receives a Holy Symbol of Talos at 25th level.
Disadvantages:
- Alignment restricted to Chaotic Neutral, Neutral Evil, or Chaotic Evil.~

@2330 = ~Divine Favor~
@2331 = ~Divine Favor
Duration: 4 rounds
Casting Time: 1

Calling upon Tyr's righteous judgment, the priest gains a scaling bonus to THAC0 and melee/ranged damage rolls (+1 at 1st level, +2 at 6th, +3 at 9th, +4 at 12th, +5 at 15th, and +6 at 18th level) for 4 rounds.~
@2332 = ~Holy Symbol of Tyr~
@2333 = ~This sacred symbol is bestowed upon faithful Priests of Tyr who reach 25th level.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Strength: +1
- Magic Resistance: +5%
- Memorize 1 extra 6th-level and 1 extra 7th-level Priest spell

Weight: 0~
@2334 = ~PRIEST OF TYR: Clerics of the Maimed God uphold justice and righteous judgment with blade and prayer.
Advantages:
- Automatically receives 1 Long Sword proficiency pip at 1st level in addition to starting proficiencies, and may equip and become proficient in Long Swords.
- May cast Divine Favor once per day at 1st level (plus 1 additional use every 5 levels): grants +1 to +6 THAC0 and damage (scaling at levels 1, 6, 9, 12, 15, and 18) for 4 rounds.
- May cast Exaltation once per day at 1st level (plus 1 additional use every 10 levels).
- Receives a Holy Symbol of Tyr at 25th level (+1 Strength, +5% Magic Resistance, +1 6th- and 7th-level Priest spell).
Disadvantages:
- Alignment restricted to Lawful Good, Lawful Neutral, or Neutral Good.~

// Component 202: Priest of Shar (@2450..@2499)
@2450 = ~priest of shar~
@2451 = ~Priest of Shar~
@2452 = ~PRIEST OF SHAR: Devotees of the Lady of Loss weave hidden strands of the Shadow Weave into divine magic, shrouding themselves in darkness and weakening foes with chilling bolts of oblivion.

Advantages:
- Automatically receives 1 Dagger proficiency at 1st level in addition to starting proficiency pips, and may equip Daggers alongside standard cleric weapons.
- Immune to Blindness.
- Shadow Weave Magic: Enemies suffer a -2 penalty to Saving Throws against all Enchantment, Illusion, and Necromancy spells cast by the Priest of Shar, as well as against Shadow Bolt.
- May cast Shadow Veil once per day at 1st level and an additional time every 5 levels thereafter, instantly gaining Improved Invisibility, Non-Detection, +4 Armor Class, and +2 to all Saving Throws for 5 rounds.
- May cast Shadow Bolt once per day at 3rd level and an additional time every 5 levels thereafter, hurling a dark bolt at a single target for 2d6 / 3d6 / 4d6 / 5d6 / 6d6 half cold and half magic damage (at levels 1 / 7 / 11 / 15 / 19; Save vs. Spell for half) and inflicting Touch of Loss (-2 THAC0 and -2 to all Saving Throws for 4 rounds on a failed Save vs. Spell).
- Receives the Holy Symbol of Shar (+1 Wisdom, +5% Magic Resistance, +1 bonus 6th- and 7th-level Priest spell) at 25th level.

Disadvantages:
- Restricted to Lawful Evil, True Neutral, Neutral Evil, or Chaotic Evil alignment.
- Requires minimum Dexterity 10 and Wisdom 9.~
@2453 = ~Shadow Veil~
@2454 = ~Shadow Veil
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: Caster
Saving Throw: None

Wraps the Priest of Shar in a silent mantle drawn from the Shadow Weave. For 5 rounds, the caster gains Improved Invisibility, Non-Detection, +4 Armor Class, and +2 to all Saving Throws.~
@2455 = ~Shadow Bolt~
@2456 = ~Shadow Bolt
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant / 4 rounds
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: Spell (half damage; negates Touch of Loss)

Launches a concentrated lance of Shadow Weave energy at a single target within 40 feet, dealing 2d6 damage at 1st level, 3d6 at 7th, 4d6 at 11th, 5d6 at 15th, and 6d6 at 19th (half cold, half magic; Save vs. Spell for half). If the target fails a Save vs. Spell, it is also afflicted with Touch of Loss, suffering -2 THAC0 and -2 to all Saving Throws for 4 rounds. Shadow Weave Magic applies an additional -2 penalty to the target's saving throws against this ability.~
@2457 = ~Holy Symbol of Shar~
@2458 = ~Holy Symbol of Shar
A smooth obsidian disc rimmed in deep violet, signifying a Priest of Shar favored by the Mistress of the Night.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Wisdom: +1
- Magic Resistance: +5%
- Memorize one extra 6th- and 7th-level Priest spell

Weight: 0~

// Component 203: Priest of Umberlee (@2500..@2549)
@2500 = ~priest of umberlee~
@2501 = ~Priest of Umberlee~
@2502 = ~PRIEST OF UMBERLEE: Devoted priests and priestesses of the Bitch Queen, the capricious goddess of the deep oceans, crushing tides, and deadly sea storms.

Advantages:
- Automatically receives 1 proficiency pip in Spears at 1st level, and may place 1 proficiency pip in Spears and Daggers as well as standard cleric weapons and fighting styles.
- Permanent +25% resistance to Cold and Electricity.
- Bonus Domain Spells: Gains Icelance (3rd level, when not already present in the Priest spellbook) and Cone of Cold (5th level) as Priest spells.
- May cast Crushing Undertow once per day at 1st level, plus an additional use every 5 levels thereafter (15-ft. enemy-only surge dealing 2d6/3d6/4d6/5d6/6d6 half-crushing, half-cold damage at levels 1/5/9/13/17 and slowing failed-save foes for 2 rounds; Save vs. Breath for half damage and to negate Slow).
- At 5th level, may invoke Tempest Shroud once per day, plus an additional use every 5 levels thereafter (5 rounds: +2 Armor Class, +50% Missile resistance, and 1d6+2 Cold damage to melee attackers).
- Receives the Holy Symbol of Umberlee at 25th level (+1 Wisdom, +5% Magic Resistance, +1 6th- and 7th-level Priest spell slot).

Disadvantages:
- Alignment restricted to Neutral Evil, Chaotic Neutral, or Chaotic Evil.
- Not available to Dwarves (unless racial kit restrictions are unlocked).~
@2503 = ~Crushing Undertow~
@2504 = ~Crushing Undertow
Range: 35 ft.
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius (enemies only)
Casting Time: 3
Saving Throw: Breath (1/2 damage; negates Slow)

Summons a crushing abyssal surge beneath target foes. Enemies caught in the blast suffer 2d6 damage at 1st level, 3d6 at 5th, 4d6 at 9th, 5d6 at 13th, and 6d6 at 17th level (half crushing, half cold; Save vs. Breath for half) and are slowed for 2 rounds unless a Save vs. Breath succeeds.~
@2505 = ~Tempest Shroud~
@2506 = ~Tempest Shroud
Range: Caster
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 1

Surrounds the Priest of Umberlee in a howling squall of freezing spray and gale-force winds, granting +2 Armor Class, +50% Missile resistance, and inflicting 1d6+2 Cold damage on any creature that strikes the caster.~
@2507 = ~Icelance~
@2508 = ~Icelance
Level: 3
Sphere: Water
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant / 3 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: Special

Hurls a jagged lance of enchanted ice at a single target, inflicting 5d6 Cold damage and stunning the target for 3 rounds unless a Save vs. Spell succeeds.~
@2509 = ~Cone of Cold~
@2510 = ~Cone of Cold
Level: 5
Sphere: Water
Range: 20 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Cone
Saving Throw: 1/2

Projects a cone of bitter frost that inflicts 10d4+10 Cold damage to all creatures within its area (Save vs. Spell for half).~
@2511 = ~Holy Symbol of Umberlee~
@2512 = ~Holy Symbol of Umberlee
This jagged shark-tooth crest of blue-green sea glass marks a favored Priest of the Bitch Queen.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Wisdom: +1
- Magic Resistance: +5%
- Memorize 1 extra 6th- and 7th-level Priest spell

Usable By:
Cleric (Neutral Evil, Chaotic Neutral, Chaotic Evil)~

// Component 204: Priest of Ilmater (@2550..@2599)
@2550 = ~priest of ilmater~
@2551 = ~Priest of Ilmater~
@2552 = ~PRIEST OF ILMATER: Selfless clerics of the Crying God who take the suffering of others upon themselves and endure wounds that would fell lesser mortals.

Advantages:
- Automatically receives 1 proficiency pip in Quarterstaffs at 1st level, and may place 1 proficiency pip in standard cleric weapons and fighting styles.
- Immune to Fatigue and gains a permanent +1 bonus to Saving Throws vs. Death.
- May invoke Ilmater's Endurance once per day at 1st level, plus an additional use every 5 levels thereafter (5 rounds: +10/+15/+20/+25 temporary maximum Hit Points at levels 1/6/11/16, immunity to Stun and Sleep/Hopelessness, and a non-additive 25% Physical Damage Resistance floor against Slashing, Crushing, Piercing, and Missile damage).
- At 3rd level, may cast Martyr's Grace once per day, plus an additional use every 5 levels thereafter (ranged ally heal restoring 3d8+6 / 4d8+8 / 5d8+10 / 6d8+12 Hit Points at levels 1/8/13/18 and curing Poison, Blindness, Deafness, and Hold, at the cost of 2d4 magic damage to the caster when current Hit Points exceed 10).
- Receives the Holy Symbol of Ilmater at 25th level (+1 Constitution, +5% Magic Resistance, +1 6th- and 7th-level Priest spell slot).

Disadvantages:
- Alignment restricted to Lawful Good, Lawful Neutral, or Neutral Good.
- Minimum Constitution: 12. Minimum Wisdom: 9.~
@2553 = ~Ilmater's Endurance~
@2554 = ~Ilmater's Endurance
Range: Caster
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 1

Channels the Crying God's steadfast resilience for 5 rounds, granting +10 temporary maximum Hit Points (+15 at 6th level, +20 at 11th, +25 at 16th), immunity to Stun, Sleep, and Hopelessness, and a non-additive 25% minimum resistance floor against Slashing, Crushing, Piercing, and Missile damage (does not stack with Armor of Faith or Hardiness).~
@2555 = ~Martyr's Grace~
@2556 = ~Martyr's Grace
Range: 30 ft.
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Casting Time: 1

Transfers an ally's suffering onto the Priest of Ilmater, restoring 3d8+6 Hit Points at 1st level (4d8+8 at 8th, 5d8+10 at 13th, and 6d8+12 at 18th) and curing Poison, Blindness, Deafness, and Hold. The caster suffers 2d4 magic damage unless at 10 Hit Points or fewer.~
@2557 = ~Holy Symbol of Ilmater~
@2558 = ~Holy Symbol of Ilmater
A pair of white hands bound at the wrists with red cord, blessed by the Broken God for his most devoted priests of Ilmater.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Constitution: +1
- Magic Resistance: +5%
- Memorize 1 extra 6th- and 7th-level Priest spell

Usable By:
Cleric (Lawful Good, Lawful Neutral, Neutral Good)~
